#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:6
msgid "Exercise: Turtle Graphics Vector"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:8
msgid ""
"In the previous exercise, you built a recursively nested `TurtleProgram` "
"using a TT muncher."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:11
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will adapt the `turtle_directions!` macro to use a "
"**Push-Down Accumulator**. Instead of nesting enum variants, your macro will "
"accumulate parsed `TurtleOp` variants in a bracketed buffer `[ $"
"($acc:expr),* ]` as it munches the input stream, ultimately constructing a "
"`Vec<TurtleOp>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:16
msgid "Instruction DSL"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:18
msgid ""
"The `turtle_directions!` macro parses the following unpunctuated commands "
"into a `Vec<TurtleOp>`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:21
msgid "`FWD n` -> `TurtleOp::Forward(n)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:22
msgid "`REV n` -> `TurtleOp::Reverse(n)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:23
msgid "`LEFT n` -> `TurtleOp::Left(n)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:24
msgid "`RIGHT n` -> `TurtleOp::Right(n)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:25
msgid "`PEN UP` -> `TurtleOp::PenUp`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:26
msgid "`PEN DOWN` -> `TurtleOp::PenDown`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:27
msgid "`RED` -> `TurtleOp::SetColor(Color::Red)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:28
msgid "`BLACK` -> `TurtleOp::SetColor(Color::Black)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:30
msgid "Instructions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:32
msgid ""
"Implement `turtle_directions!` using internal rule push-down accumulation."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:33
msgid "Evaluate to `vec![ ... ]` when all tokens have been consumed."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:52
msgid ""
"// TODO: Implement the `turtle_directions!` macro using a push-down "
"accumulator.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators/exercise.md:85
msgid ""
"Explain why push-down accumulation is necessary when building flat "
"collections like a `Vec<T>` or array: individual macro recursive calls "
"cannot emit loose comma-separated list fragments into surrounding "
"expressions without storing them inside a container/buffer parameter like `[$"
"($acc:expr),*]`."
msgstr ""
